<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Hashim Thaci's second conviction in The Hague reignites debate in Kosovo about justice and the Kosovo Specialist Chambers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e014b7423cb38cff310322751cc3c2f0d630cd9bf5362d346f4f31754d33b0fe</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T20:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hashim-thaci-s-second-conviction-in-the-hague-reignites-debate-in-kosovo-about-justice-and-the-kosov/a-79975227--3db3936546e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hashim-thaci-s-second-conviction-in-the-hague-reignites-debate-in-kosovo-about-justice-and-the-kosovo-specialist-chambers/a-79975227?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former President Hashim Thaci has been convicted of trying to influence witnesses in his war crimes trial. The conviction has reignited debate in Kosovo about the Kosovo Specialist Chambers, the court that convicted him.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Back to 1997: Russia wants NATO to roll back its eastern expansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09d71c53aec2e6ab32f8bce0df536743f646c3819dc4fe015fdd950289c5e3a0</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/back-to-1997-russia-wants-nato-to-roll-back-its-eastern-expansion/a-79970289--e5e38f4e75de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/back-to-1997-russia-wants-nato-to-roll-back-its-eastern-expansion/a-79970289?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Kremlin is reportedly calling on NATO to withdraw from large parts of Eastern Europe. What this would mean for the security of millions of Europeans — and what lies behind Russia's plan.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Rights court rules Turkey must release jailed lawmaker Atalay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8996862f039e765b18e6114dfc2e33228b35d4f4edd6757a365f328e5e285ef8</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rights-court-rules-turkey-must-release-jailed-lawmaker-atalay/a-79972462--8247972e6110.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rights-court-rules-turkey-must-release-jailed-lawmaker-atalay/a-79972462?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Court of Human Rights has called for the release of imprisoned elected lawmaker Can Atalay. Atalay has been in prison for almost five years despite rulings from the Turkish Constitutional Court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Students' List candidates take seats as Serbian parliament opens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b76dc6148e2d6dede8041ad955c818a088a74c537310cec4a92a4751b48a76b</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/students-list-candidates-take-seats-as-serbian-parliament-opens/a-79969166--96de93cfad7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/students-list-candidates-take-seats-as-serbian-parliament-opens/a-79969166?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Serbia's Student List's candidates have taken their oaths in the inaugural parliament session. As the new majority, they have 90 days to form a government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Despite restrictive abortion laws, Poland's 'Abortomat' — a locker that dispenses abortion pills — helps women who want to end a pregnancy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f100b3ba3cbce90987d6fb0799336d04a1f03582342b0e8080361f2c486e7d9</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/polish-activists-face-opposition-as-they-make-abortion-more-accessible/a-79943914--39db4083c558.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/despite-restrictive-abortion-laws-poland-s-abortomat-a-locker-that-dispenses-abortion-pills-helps-women-who-want-to-end-a-pregnancy/a-79943914?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abortion laws in Poland are very restrictive. Activists there have found a new way to help women wanting to terminate a pregnancy: the "Abortomat," a locker that dispenses abortion pills. But they face fierce opposition.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelenskyy says security deal could go to referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:185a8a7cb76437d8ed9bbadf32ef11edf8c53604936ff387803751756eafa700</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535--17ea05d7ca0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has broached the idea of Kyiv giving up the Donbas region in exchange for NATO membership, the Ukrainian president said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey uses espionage accusations to pressure government critics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c39809db485e1574f7415989bea99fb2f7bb42da0b31fcaec6ab1ae433476597</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T07:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-uses-espionage-accusations-to-pressure-government-critics/a-79943768--a2686613e6a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-uses-espionage-accusations-to-pressure-government-critics/a-79943768?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of a German foundation's employee in Istanbul this week has put the focus back on pressure tactics used by the Erdogan administration. The arrest is far from the first of its kind.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests: Do Baby Boomers really have it better than young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d69101bb28fce3cd7d7a0e73e74374509fa95923943eeefa7ad13f4a7707c9dd</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854--e581c42657a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Should young people in Germany be more worried about their future than Baby Boomers were in the 1980s and 1990s? Or should both generations take to the streets and protest together? DW checked the data.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The dangers of revising Europe's security architecture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65bd77d48b864e5aaf1b7b133e3eb9202da7360fd8cade7d6ca02440f20523da</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049--ae25152ee718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts warn against revising Europe's security framework because they say it would mean granting Moscow its longstanding wish of renegotiating postwar security on the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia braces for massive protest against public media reform plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a481525c2752470896ca2d300c2be5ff7e933d8c9d174f54baaeec72f15d05c</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533--a08ee7cdb27e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fast-tracked bill to cut public media funding has sparked strikes, rallies and fears for the independence of public broadcasting in Czechia. A massive protest is planned for Prague on Sunday.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders tussle over whom to send to Ukraine, Russia peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:514d7893eb074531e4332d835f022089c45b58d0dbd1ae115c53f32c15863080</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468--127d08162dcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A seat at the table for Europe now appears likely following comments by a US envoy who just held talks with Putin. But who will take that seat remains unclear.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can the EU make it harder to trick consumers online?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2924a3ffcc66eb0f2cd36c63857202f63cdd1da68c62bc86bbcab1b1d877a876</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447--856c99598d6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to curb subscription traps, misleading sales tactics and features that keep people scrolling. What would the proposed Digital Fairness Act change, and does it go far enough?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What have the talks with Russia and the US in Abu Dhabi achieved for Ukraine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae1ac89caae18aaa3513e845de82aa51b8602ea7a717d83aee50cd72cf623512</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613--89b8a9b8f641.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first trilateral talks between Ukraine, the US and Russia in nine months have ended with an agreement on exchanging prisoners. Does this mark a genuine breakthrough and a step toward peace?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary eases abortion restrictions in women's rights overhaul</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a73cc9799d764d2342e43643719756afa9da372af5326a78622085c6037a1136</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-rules/a-79931614--3bb42fe8feff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-restrictions-in-women-s-rights-overhaul/a-79931614?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The reforms mark a break the the conservative policies of former PM Viktor Orban. The controversial "heartbeat regulation" is to be scrapped and women are to be better protected against violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK court convicts 2 Iranian men of spying on journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddfa3c793b5855ce23773e5bf75424c9032d45ed6318d5724fefb352bd883d56</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583--9da85f420d5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has found two Iranian citizens guilty of surveilling reporters for a Persian-language television station critical of Iran's government. One was also convicted of planning a violent attack against them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0c8e1ae31687e027e8ec015701119296dfd701fff57a62b93166c0127b11f1a</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>British counterterrorism police arrest US soldier accused of spying on behalf of Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a20200d8016c6678d066f26394cc6328be6d2ef659e8ad1274b570436b678060</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240--5991e0a904a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A member of the US Army has been arrested near Gloucester in England. Police said he was suspected of espionage activity in connection with Russia. Investigators from the US and UK are involved in the probe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK Privy Council overrules Trinidad and Tobago gay sex law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23f3cb655cfd84f9e924c05d8355b23b234e2b29a05609e856fa41faa038bf7e</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163--f186aba38925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has overturned a Trinidad and Tobago law criminalizing consensual sexual relations between male same-sex couples. As a result of the colonial legacy, it is the independent country's last court of appeal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Victims of Nazi war in Poland call on Germany for support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2da168206faf9b7f42074f174b73d21c34f9a7224f850cc417df24bb79beb79f</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311--36756d6320e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 80 years after the end of World War II, Polish victims of the Nazi regime are still waiting for a "humanitarian gesture" from Germany. The 2027 draft budget hasn't left them much hope for possible reparations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran denies role in fridge hack, France summons ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f46dbdfe588369e4ecfb1491184df28096676b61e9014192d4644eecb0b73bd</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206--6d0355211a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France has said it rules "nothing" out in response to a cyberattack on supermarket refrigeration units. Iran, however, said it categorically rejected Paris' "baseless and one-sided accusations" of IRGC involvement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
